<task id="032" project="spaarkeai-compose-r6">
  <metadata>
    <title>Endpoint + client wiring for template selection/merge</title>
    <phase>3 Template part-merge</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 031</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies `.cs` (Compose endpoint) AND `.tsx` (Compose client) on the `bff-api` + frontend hot path — end-to-end wiring of the template-merge capability across the BFF/client boundary. FULL per root CLAUDE.md §8 (modifying `.cs`/`.tsx`, tags include `compose`/`frontend`). Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check run.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Wiring over a finished engine (030) + storage path (031): add a Compose endpoint that invokes the merge and a client affordance to select/apply a firm/matter template. The hard judgment is upstream; this is well-specified integration. Sonnet per plan.md §5 Phase 3.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches `Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs` + `Services/Compose/` + the Compose client (`Spaarke.Compose.Components`) — the most-contested BFF + client surface, actively edited by `spaarkeai-compose-r5` (`ComposeService.cs`/`ComposeWorkspace.tsx`), `r4.5`, `r1/r2/r3`, `spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2`, and `agreements-r1`/`analysis-hub-r1`. Serialize Compose-file edits; sequential after 031; `/conflict-check` before the PR; NEVER delete `docxBridge.ts`.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>031</deps>
    <tags>bff,compose,frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-1.5 days</estimated-effort>
